#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "A rider on the road"
msgstr "Seorang penunggang kuda di jalan"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Quraysh had offered a reward for each of the two travellers. Suraqah ibn Malik recounts that a man came to his gathering and said he had just seen figures near the coast. Suraqah recognised who they must be, and set out after them."
msgstr "Quraisy telah menawarkan hadiah untuk masing-masing dari kedua musafir tersebut. Suraqah ibn Malik menceritakan bahwa seorang pria datang ke tempat perkumpulannya dan berkata bahwa ia baru saja melihat sosok-sosok di dekat pantai. Suraqah mengenali siapa mereka sebenarnya, lalu berangkat mengejar mereka."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "By his own account, he came close enough to hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. Then the forelegs of his horse sank into the ground up to the knees, and he was thrown from it."
msgstr "Menurut pengakuannya sendiri, ia datang cukup dekat hingga mendengar Nabi ﷺ membaca Al-Qur'an. Kemudian kaki depan kudanya terperosok ke dalam tanah hingga ke lutut, dan ia terjatuh darinya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "He told them what Quraysh intended and offered them provisions. They took nothing from him and asked only that he keep their news hidden. At his request, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety on a piece of leather. Then they went on."
msgstr "Ia memberi tahu mereka apa yang direncanakan Quraisy dan menawarkan perbekalan kepada mereka. Mereka tidak mengambil apa pun darinya dan hanya meminta agar ia merahasiakan kabar mereka. Atas permintaannya, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah menuliskan jaminan keamanan untuknya di selembar kulit. Kemudian mereka melanjutkan perjalanan."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Quba: the first stop"
msgstr "Quba: pemberhentian pertama"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "He stayed among them for more than ten nights. There he founded the mosque that the account calls the one founded on piety, and he prayed in it."
msgstr "Beliau tinggal di antara mereka selama lebih dari sepuluh malam. Di sana beliau mendirikan masjid yang dalam riwayat disebut sebagai masjid yang didirikan atas dasar takwa, dan beliau salat di dalamnya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Then he rode on, with people walking beside him, until his camel knelt at a place in Madinah where some of the Muslims already prayed. It was a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "Kemudian beliau berkendara lagi, dengan orang-orang berjalan di sampingnya, hingga untanya berlutut di suatu tempat di Madinah tempat beberapa orang Muslim biasa salat. Tempat itu adalah tempat penjemuran kurma."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Suraqah’s account records the reward offered for each of the two, and a report that figures had been seen near the coast."
msgstr "Riwayat Suraqah mencatat hadiah yang ditawarkan untuk masing-masing dari keduanya, dan laporan bahwa sosok-sosok telah terlihat di dekat pantai."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not establish where on the route this happened, and the scene does not place it."
msgstr "Riwayat ini tidak menetapkan di mana peristiwa ini terjadi di sepanjang rute tersebut, dan visualnya tidak menentukannya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Suraqah describes the forelegs of his horse sinking into the ground to the knees, and being thrown."
msgstr "Suraqah menceritakan bahwa kaki depan kudanya terperosok ke dalam tanah hingga ke lutut, lalu ia terjatuh."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This is his own first-person account. The scene shows the road, not the event or any person."
msgstr "Ini adalah kesaksian orang pertama dari dirinya sendiri. Visual tersebut menunjukkan jalan, bukan peristiwa atau orang tertentu."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They asked only that he keep their news hidden; ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah wrote him a guarantee of safety."
msgstr "Mereka hanya meminta agar ia merahasiakan kabar mereka; ‘Amir bin Fuhayrah kemudian menuliskan surat jaminan keamanan untuknya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The wording of the written guarantee is not given in this passage."
msgstr "Redaksi surat jaminan keamanan tersebut tidak disebutkan dalam bagian ini."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The account gives a stay of more than ten nights among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf and the founding of a mosque there."
msgstr "Riwayat tersebut menyebutkan masa tinggal selama lebih dari sepuluh malam di kalangan Bani ‘Amr bin ‘Awf dan pembangunan sebuah masjid di sana."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "He rode on with people walking beside him until his camel knelt at the site of the mosque in Madinah."
msgstr "Beliau berkendara dengan orang-orang yang berjalan di sisinya hingga untanya menderum di lokasi masjid di Madinah."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not establish the route taken through the town or the appearance of the place."
msgstr "Riwayat ini tidak menetapkan rute yang dilewati di dalam kota maupun rupa dari tempat tersebut."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "<0>Play</0> walks the chapter stage by stage with AI-generated narration."
msgstr "<0>Putar</0> menelusuri bab ini tahap demi tahap dengan narasi yang dihasilkan AI."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "<0>Play</0> walks the chapter stage by stage. The captions keep time over a quiet wind."
msgstr "<0>Putar</0> menelusuri bab ini tahap demi tahap. Teks takarir menyelaraskan waktu diiringi suara angin yang tenang."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "<0>Ask</0> uses the chapter’s context to research in Turath and answer with source citations."
msgstr "<0>Tanya</0> menggunakan konteks bab ini untuk meneliti dalam Turath dan menjawab lengkap dengan kutipan sumber."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This excerpt does not give an exact departure date."
msgstr "Kutipan ini tidak menyebutkan tanggal keberangkatan yang pasti."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt describes preparations, not a nightly delivery to the cave."
msgstr "Kutipan ini menggambarkan persiapan, bukan pengantaran setiap malam ke gua."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt does not describe erasing footprints."
msgstr "Kutipan ini tidak menggambarkan penghapusan jejak kaki."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The account does not describe the cave’s dimensions or layout."
msgstr "Riwayat ini tidak menggambarkan ukuran atau tata letak gua tersebut."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This excerpt is not the full verse and does not itself name Abu Bakr or Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Kutipan ini bukanlah ayat yang lengkap dan tidak menyebutkan nama Abu Bakar atau Gunung Thawr secara langsung."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s commentary, not the Quranic wording itself."
msgstr "Ini adalah tafsir Ibnu Katsir, bukan redaksi Al-Qur'an itu sendiri."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "It does not give an exact location for the stay among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."
msgstr "Riwayat ini tidak memberikan lokasi pasti mengenai tempat tinggal di kalangan Bani ‘Amr bin ‘Awf."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The passage does not name the place; identifying it as Quba rests on other reports."
msgstr "Bagian teks ini tidak menyebutkan nama tempat tersebut; penetapannya sebagai Quba bersandar pada riwayat-riwayat lain."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The night of departure"
msgstr "Malam keberangkatan"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The leaders of Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled their affairs, to decide what to do about the Prophet ﷺ now that they feared him."
msgstr "Para pemimpin Quraisy berkumpul di Darun Nadwah, tempat mereka biasa memutuskan urusan mereka, untuk menentukan apa yang harus dilakukan terhadap Nabi ﷺ setelah mereka merasa terancam oleh beliau."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "That night they gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak, and assured him that no harm from them would reach him."
msgstr "Malam itu mereka berkumpul di depan pintunya, menunggu beliau tidur. Beliau menyuruh ‘Ali untuk berbaring di tempat tidurnya dengan berselimutkan jubah hijaunya, dan meyakinkannya bahwa tidak akan ada bahaya dari mereka yang dapat menyentuhnya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "‘Ali stayed behind for another reason too. People in Makkah left their valuables with the Prophet ﷺ for safekeeping, because they knew his honesty. ‘Ali was to return every one of them."
msgstr "‘Ali tetap tinggal di belakang karena alasan lain juga. Orang-orang di Makkah biasa menitipkan barang-barang berharga mereka kepada Nabi ﷺ untuk diamankan, karena mereka mengetahui kejujuran beliau. ‘Ali bertugas untuk mengembalikan setiap barang tersebut kepada pemiliknya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The tent of Umm Ma‘bad"
msgstr "Kemah Umm Ma‘bad"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Further on they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad of Khuza‘ah and asked for hospitality. She had no food to offer, she said, and no ewe but one that gave no milk."
msgstr "Lebih jauh lagi, mereka singgah di kemah Umm Ma‘bad dari suku Khuza‘ah dan meminta dijamu. Ia berkata bahwa ia tidak memiliki makanan untuk disuguhkan, dan tidak ada domba betina kecuali satu yang tidak menghasilkan susu."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ called for the ewe, passed his hand over its udder and called on Allah. He milked it into a large vessel until it frothed, and said: drink, Umm Ma‘bad. Ibn Kathir notes that her story is well known and comes through routes that strengthen one another."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ meminta domba betina tersebut, mengusap kantong susunya dengan tangan beliau, dan berdoa kepada Allah. Beliau memerah susunya ke dalam wadah besar hingga berbuih, lalu bersabda: minumlah, wahai Umm Ma‘bad. Ibnu Katsir mencatat bahwa kisahnya sangat terkenal dan diriwayatkan melalui jalur-jalur yang saling menguatkan satu sama lain."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq reports that Quraysh met in Dar al-Nadwah to consult about the Prophet ﷺ once they feared him."
msgstr "Ibnu Ishaq meriwayatkan bahwa Quraisy berkumpul di Darun Nadwah untuk bermusyawarah mengenai Nabi ﷺ setelah mereka merasa terancam oleh beliau."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The excerpt covers the meeting, not what was said in it."
msgstr "Kutipan ini membahas tentang pertemuan tersebut, bukan apa yang diucapkan di dalamnya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They gathered at his door at night; he told ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak and assured him of safety."
msgstr "Mereka berkumpul di depan pintunya pada malam hari; beliau menyuruh ‘Ali tidur di tempat tidurnya di bawah jubah hijaunya dan menjamin keamanannya."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Kathir notes that al-Waqidi also relates this, combining several narrators’ accounts."
msgstr "Ibnu Katsir mencatat bahwa al-Waqidi juga meriwayatkan hal ini, dengan menggabungkan riwayat dari beberapa perawi."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq introduces this with “as it has reached me”."
msgstr "Ibnu Ishaq mengawali kisah ini dengan kalimat \"sebagaimana yang telah sampai kepadaku\"."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They stopped at Umm Ma‘bad’s tent; she had only a ewe without milk, which then gave milk in abundance."
msgstr "Mereka singgah di kemah Umm Ma‘bad; ia hanya memiliki seekor domba betina yang tidak menghasilkan susu, yang kemudian mengeluarkan susu dengan melimpah."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Kathir calls the story well known, through routes that support one another. It does not fix where the tent stood."
msgstr "Ibnu Katsir menyebut kisah ini sangat terkenal, melalui jalur-jalur yang saling mendukung satu sama lain. Kisah ini tidak menetapkan di mana kemah tersebut berdiri."

#: src/content/details.js
#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"
msgstr "Al-Rahiq al-Makhtum"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The noon visit"
msgstr "Kunjungan di waktu siang"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "At the height of noon, an hour at which he never used to come, the Prophet ﷺ arrived at Abu Bakr’s house with his face covered. He said he had been given permission to leave. Abu Bakr asked to go with him, and he said yes."
msgstr "Di terik tengah hari, waktu yang tidak biasa baginya untuk berkunjung, Nabi ﷺ tiba di rumah Abu Bakar dengan wajah tertutup. Beliau mengabarkan bahwa beliau telah diizinkan untuk pergi. Abu Bakar meminta untuk menemani beliau, dan beliau pun mengiyakannya."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is ‘Aishah’s account as quoted in a modern sirah. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Ini adalah riwayat ‘Aisyah sebagaimana dikutip dalam sirah modern. Posisi rumah ini hanya sebagai ilustrasi."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Stones in the niche"
msgstr "Batu di dalam ceruk"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him, five or six thousand dirhams. Asma recounts that her blind grandfather feared the family had been left with nothing. She put stones where the money used to be kept, covered them with a cloth, and guided his hand to them so that he would be at ease."
msgstr "Abu Bakar membawa seluruh uangnya, sekitar lima atau enam ribu dirham. Asma menceritakan bahwa kakeknya yang buta khawatir keluarga yang ditinggalkan tidak memiliki apa-apa lagi. Asma meletakkan batu-batu di tempat biasa uang disimpan, menutupinya dengan sehelai kain, lalu menuntun tangan kakeknya untuk meraba batu-batu tersebut agar hatinya tenang."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Reported by Ibn Ishaq from Asma through her grandson. The position of the house is illustrative."
msgstr "Diriwayatkan oleh Ibnu Ishaq dari Asma melalui cucunya. Posisi rumah ini hanya sebagai ilustrasi."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Why south?"
msgstr "Mengapa ke selatan?"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Madinah lies to the north, and that is where a search would begin. They left in the opposite direction, on the road towards Yemen, for about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah berada di sebelah utara, dan ke sanalah pencarian akan dimulai. Mereka pergi ke arah yang berlawanan, menyusuri jalan menuju Yaman, sejauh sekitar lima mil hingga mencapai Bukit Thawr."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is a modern author’s reading of the route, not wording from an early report."
msgstr "Ini adalah penafsiran penulis modern mengenai rute tersebut, bukan redaksi dari riwayat awal."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "She of the two belts"
msgstr "Pemilik dua sabuk"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "When the three nights had passed, Asma brought their provisions but had forgotten a strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and used it. For that she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn, she of the two belts."
msgstr "Setelah tiga malam berlalu, Asma membawakan perbekalan untuk mereka tetapi lupa membawa tali untuk menggantung kantong makanan tersebut. Ia melepas sabuk pinggangnya dan menggunakannya sebagai tali. Karena hal itu, ia dijuluki Dhat al-Nitaqayn, si pemilik dua sabuk."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. ‘Aishah’s account in al-Bukhari places the belt at the packing of the provisions instead."
msgstr "Riwayat Ibnu Ishaq. Riwayat ‘Aisyah dalam al-Bukhari menyebutkan bahwa sabuk tersebut digunakan saat mengemas perbekalan."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The spider’s web"
msgstr "Sarang laba-laba"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "One report says the pursuers climbed the mountain, passed the cave, and saw a spider’s web across its opening. No one could have gone in, they reasoned, and they moved on. Ibn Kathir calls its chain good, the best of what is reported on this. The scene does not draw the web."
msgstr "Satu riwayat menyebutkan bahwa para pengejar mendaki gunung, melewati gua, dan melihat sarang laba-laba di mulut gua. Mereka berpikir tidak mungkin ada orang yang masuk ke dalam, lalu mereka pun pergi. Ibnu Katsir menyebut sanad riwayat ini baik, dan merupakan yang terbaik dari apa yang diriwayatkan tentang peristiwa ini. Visual ini tidak menggambarkan sarang laba-laba tersebut."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A single report. The nesting doves of popular retellings are not part of it."
msgstr "Riwayat tunggal. Burung merpati yang bersarang dalam cerita populer bukan bagian dari riwayat ini."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The stations of the road"
msgstr "Persinggahan di sepanjang jalan"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the way the guide took: below Makkah, along the coast, across the road below ‘Usfan, below Amaj, past Qudayd, then al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf and on. Many of these names are hard to place today, so the line drawn here stays approximate."
msgstr "Ibnu Ishaq menyebutkan rute yang diambil oleh pemandu: di bawah Makkah, menyusuri pantai, menyeberangi jalan di bawah 'Usfan, di bawah Amaj, melewati Qudayd, lalu al-Kharrar, Thaniyyat al-Marah, Liqf, dan seterusnya. Banyak dari nama-nama ini yang sulit dipastikan lokasinya saat ini, sehingga garis yang digambarkan di sini tetap berupa perkiraan."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A list of names, without distances or days."
msgstr "Daftar nama tempat, tanpa rincian jarak atau hari."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "White garments"
msgstr "Pakaian putih"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "On the way they met al-Zubayr with a group of Muslim merchants returning from Syria. He gave the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr white garments to wear."
msgstr "Di tengah perjalanan, mereka bertemu al-Zubayr bersama rombongan pedagang Muslim yang baru kembali dari Syam. Ia memberikan pakaian putih kepada Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakar untuk dikenakan."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "From al-Bukhari, as quoted by Ibn Kathir. The account does not say where on the road they met."
msgstr "Dari al-Bukhari, sebagaimana dikutip oleh Ibnu Katsir. Riwayat ini tidak menyebutkan di bagian jalan mana mereka bertemu."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The first Friday"
msgstr "Jumat pertama"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "After leaving Quba, the time for Friday prayer came while he was among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf. He led it there, in the mosque in the bed of the valley, with about a hundred men."
msgstr "Setelah meninggalkan Quba, waktu salat Jumat tiba saat beliau berada di tengah-tengah Bani Salim bin 'Awf. Beliau memimpin salat di sana, di masjid yang berada di dasar lembah, bersama sekitar seratus orang laki-laki."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Quoted from a modern sirah, which cites Ibn Hisham. The position is illustrative."
msgstr "Dikutip dari sirah modern, yang merujuk pada Ibnu Hisyam. Posisi ini hanya sebagai ilustrasi."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Let her go"
msgstr "Biarkan dia berjalan"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Clan after clan took hold of his camel’s rope and invited him to stay with them. Each time he answered: let her go, for she is under command. She walked on until she knelt in the quarter of Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Kabilah demi kabilah memegang tali kendali unta beliau dan mengundang beliau untuk tinggal bersama mereka. Setiap kali beliau menjawab: biarkan dia berjalan, karena ia sedang diperintah. Unta itu terus berjalan hingga akhirnya menderum di wilayah Bani Malik bin al-Najjar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s report. Her path through the town is not known."
msgstr "Riwayat Ibnu Ishaq. Jalur yang dilewati unta tersebut di dalam kota tidak diketahui."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The house of Abu Ayyub"
msgstr "Rumah Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "He stayed in the house of Abu Ayyub until his mosque and his rooms were built, and he worked on the building himself alongside the Muhajirun and the Ansar."
msgstr "Beliau tinggal di rumah Abu Ayyub sampai masjid dan kamar-kamar beliau selesai dibangun, dan beliau ikut bekerja membangunnya sendiri bersama kaum Muhajirin dan Ansar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The house is placed beside the mosque site for illustration."
msgstr "Rumah ini ditempatkan di samping lokasi masjid sebagai ilustrasi."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "Brothers"
msgstr "Mempersaudarakan"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "He paired those who had migrated with those who received them, as brothers, so that each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Beliau mempersaudarakan orang-orang yang berhijrah dengan orang-orang yang menyambut mereka, sehingga setiap pendatang baru memiliki seseorang untuk bersandar."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "This is Ibn Kathir’s chapter heading. The individual pairings are listed in the pages that follow it."
msgstr "Ini adalah judul bab dari Ibnu Katsir. Nama-nama pasangan yang dipersaudarakan tercantum di halaman-halaman setelahnya."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The full moon has risen"
msgstr "Telah terbit bulan purnama"

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "A well-known report says the women and children sang “The full moon has risen upon us, from the passes of al-Wada‘” when he arrived. Al-Bayhaqi relates it from Ibn ‘Aishah, a later narrator, not from someone who was there."
msgstr "Sebuah riwayat terkenal menyebutkan bahwa kaum wanita dan anak-anak menyanyikan \"Tala'al badru 'alayna, min tsaniyyatil-wada'\" ketika beliau tiba. Al-Bayhaqi meriwayatkannya dari Ibnu 'Aisyah, seorang perawi belakangan, bukan dari seseorang yang hadir di sana."

#: src/content/details.js
#, ai
msgid "The chain stops short of an eyewitness, and some place the song at a later return to Madinah, not at this arrival."
msgstr "Silsilah sanadnya terputus sebelum saksi mata, dan beberapa pihak menempatkan nyanyian tersebut pada kepulangan berikutnya ke Madinah, bukan pada kedatangan kali ini."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "Along the way"
msgstr "Di sepanjang jalan"

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
#, ai
msgid "Close detail"
msgstr "Tutup detail"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Leaving Makkah"
msgstr "Meninggalkan Makkah"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Night of 27 Safar · 12–13 September 622"
msgstr "Malam 27 Safar · 12–13 September 622"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The night of departure is in the accounts. Its place in the calendar is a modern reckoning."
msgstr "Malam keberangkatan disebutkan dalam riwayat. Posisinya dalam kalender adalah perhitungan modern."

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday"
msgstr "Malam-malam sebelum Jumat, Sabtu, dan Ahad"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Three nights is in al-Bukhari. Naming them after the days of the week follows a modern reckoning."
msgstr "Tiga malam disebutkan dalam al-Bukhari. Penamaannya berdasarkan hari dalam sepekan mengikuti perhitungan modern."

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The guide arrives"
msgstr "Pemandu jalan tiba"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Night of Monday, 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 September 622"
msgstr "Malam Senin, 1 Rabi'ul Awwal · 16 September 622"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The guide came with the two mounts after the third night, as arranged. The calendar date is a modern reckoning."
msgstr "Pemandu jalan datang membawa kedua hewan tunggangan setelah malam ketiga, sesuai kesepakatan. Tanggal kalender adalah perhitungan modern."

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "On the coastal road"
msgstr "Di jalan pesisir"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "About a week"
msgstr "Sekitar sepekan"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The accounts give the order of what happened on the road, but no days. The pursuit and the tent of Umm Ma‘bad fall somewhere in this week."
msgstr "Riwayat-riwayat menyebutkan urutan kejadian di perjalanan, tetapi tidak menyebutkan harinya. Pengejaran dan tenda Ummu Ma'bad terjadi di suatu waktu dalam pekan ini."

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Arrival at Quba"
msgstr "Tiba di Quba"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Monday · 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 September 622"
msgstr "Senin · 8 Rabi'ul Awwal · 23 September 622"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The account in al-Bukhari says it was a Monday in Rabi‘ al-Awwal. The day of the month is a modern reckoning."
msgstr "Catatan dalam al-Bukhari menyebutkan bahwa itu terjadi pada hari Senin di bulan Rabi'ul Awwal. Tanggal dalam bulan tersebut merupakan perhitungan modern."

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The stay at Quba"
msgstr "Masa tinggal di Quba"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Four days, or more than ten nights"
msgstr "Empat hari, atau lebih dari sepuluh malam"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Ibn Ishaq gives Monday to Thursday. The report in al-Bukhari says more than ten nights, and Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf said eighteen. Ibn Kathir sets the reports side by side without settling it."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menyebutkan hari Senin hingga Kamis. Riwayat dalam al-Bukhari menyebutkan lebih dari sepuluh malam, dan Bani 'Amr ibn 'Awf menyebutkan delapan belas hari. Ibn Kathir menyandingkan riwayat-riwayat tersebut tanpa menetapkan mana yang paling kuat."

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "The first Friday, and Madinah"
msgstr "Jumat pertama, dan Madinah"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Friday · 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Jumat · 12 Rabi'ul Awwal · 27 September 622"

#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "That it was a Friday is in the early reports. The calendar date is a modern reckoning, and it follows the four-day stay."
msgstr "Bahwa hari itu adalah hari Jumat disebutkan dalam riwayat-riwayat awal. Tanggal kalender merupakan perhitungan modern, dan ini mengikuti masa tinggal selama empat hari."

